sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Source as Source
    participant Orbital as Orbital + Taxi
    participant Publisher as Publish bridge
    participant Rabbit as RabbitMQ
    participant Worker as Route worker
    participant Target as HTTP target

    alt Adobe-origin ingress
        Source->>Orbital: Submit Adobe<br/>customer update
        Orbital->>Orbital: Resolve facts and<br/>project SAP IDoc
        Orbital->>Publisher: POST projected IDoc<br/>+ lineage
        Publisher->>Rabbit: Mandatory persistent<br/>publish
        Rabbit-->>Publisher: Confirm routable<br/>publication
        Publisher-->>Orbital: 202 Accepted
        Orbital-->>Source: 202 Accepted
    else SAP-origin test ingress
        Source->>Rabbit: Publish SAP XML<br/>+ lineage metadata
        Rabbit-->>Source: Confirm accepted<br/>publication
    end

    Note over Rabbit,Target: RabbitMQ creates one independent queue copy<br/>for every configured target route.

    Rabbit->>Worker: Deliver one route copy<br/>(manual ACK)
    Worker->>Worker: Validate metadata and<br/>adapt XML / JSON

    alt Message validation fails
        Worker-->>Rabbit: Reject without requeue
        Rabbit->>Rabbit: Dead-letter only this route copy
    else Message is valid
        Worker->>Orbital: Invoke route-specific<br/>saved query
        Orbital->>Target: Write projected<br/>target request

        alt Target and query return 2xx
            Target-->>Orbital: 2xx response
            Orbital-->>Worker: 2xx response
            Worker-->>Rabbit: ACK route copy
        else Downstream processing fails
            Orbital-->>Worker: Error / non-2xx
            Worker-->>Rabbit: Reject without requeue
            Rabbit->>Rabbit: Dead-letter only this route copy
        end
    end

    Note over Source,Target: Adobe → SAP is the exception: its queue is the simulated target.<br/>No consumer is attached, so the message remains available for inspection.
